    "shadow": "Too much, and creativity can scatter into endless beginnings that never finish. Or your worth can become fused with what you make, so every piece becomes a verdict. The muse turns into a harsh critic.",
    "void": "When creativity goes quiet, life can feel flat and borrowed. Often it's been shamed out, or crowded out, rather than lost. The longing to make something is the part of you that hasn't forgotten.",
